* `guestC : Cfg`: the type table `guestT`, the typed globals `guestGT` (every one-word guest
  global except the three allocator pointers; buffers and records typed, the rest `scalar`),
  the protected globals `guestPG` and the union tags `guestTags` (MPT nodes, tag = `NODE_KIND`).
* `ty_*` lemmas (`guestC.ty tEV = evTy`, by `rfl`) and `cfgOK_guest : CfgOK guestC`.

Layout decisions (byte offset / slot):
* `EV` (scratch, 280 B): `prot` = STACK 1, SP 2, MEM 3, MEM_LEN 4, MEM_CAP 5 (stack/memory hook,
  ms-struct), GAS_LEFT 8, RUNNING 13, STATE_GAS_SPILLED 24, STACK_CAP 29 (Φ / chain,
  ms-frames), RETDATA 18, RETDATA_CAP 27 (`set_retdata` reuses its buffer), STACK_MARK 26,
  MEM_MARK 28 (frame release), and LOGS 11, MSG 14, DELETE 17 (frame-local objects in the
  child's scratch, dropped from `Γ` by the release; ms-frames). Typed: ACC_ADDRS 21
  `ptr HTh20` / ACC_KEYS 22 `ptr HTh52`. All other slots `scalar`. Untagged.
* `CK` (scratch, 104 B): all `prot` (frame driver only). `MSGh` / `MSGs` (heap / scratch,
  176 B): MSG_ACC_ADDRS 19 `ptr HTh20` / MSG_ACC_KEYS 20 `ptr HTh52`, all else `scalar`.
* Hash tables: a table is a header plus its arrays, all `prot`. Header types are split by key
  length (`htKL`): `HTh20/28/32/52/60` (heap), `HTs20` (scratch), `HTt20` (heap, values are
  `HTh32` tables); the value kind of a header type is `htVal`. Heap arrays have the
  owner-encoded type `tOwn T` (interface rev. 6), scratch arrays `HTAs`; `HTAh` is unused.
* Lists: header `LSTh` / `LSTs` plus array `LSTAh` / `LSTAs`, all `prot`.
* MPT nodes `NHASHED` / `NLEAF` / `NEXT` / `NBRANCH` (heap), slot 0 (`NODE_KIND`) `prot` and
  tagged; child slots `uptr` of the four.
* `Bn`: an `n`-byte all-`scalar` heap buffer (global scratch buffers and tables).
* Globals that are 0 until after main's init prefix (`ev`, `cur_cont`, `ws`, `bs`, `ts`,
  `journal`, `sk_buf`, `bal_*`) are `nptr`.
-/

